# Change completion

Do not mark a change complete until all steps below pass.

## 1. Document the change

Add or update a file under `docs/` for every non-trivial change. See `docs/changes/README.md`.

Each change doc must include:

- **Product:** what users see, demo impact, and why the change matters
- **Technical:** files touched, data/query/schema impact, setup or wiring changes

Prefer `docs/changes/YYYY-MM-DD-short-slug.md` for discrete changes. Update existing docs (for example `GETTING_STARTED.md`, `CONCEPTS.md`) when setup or architecture changes.

Use STE per `.cursor/rules/technical-english.mdc`.

## 2. Run tests

Run commands that match the change scope:

| Scope | Commands |
|-------|----------|
| Any code change | `npm test` |
| TypeScript / lint | `npm run lint` |
| Build surface | `npm run build` |
| Full gate | `npm run verify` (lint + test + build) |
| UI / Migration Pulse | `npm run dev` — confirm in Fabric App embed (`fabricEmbedded=true`) |
| DAX change | `node node_modules/@microsoft/fabric-app-data-cli/dist/index.js query migrationPulse --query "..."` |

Default: run `npm run verify` plus any scope-specific commands above.

## 3. Thermo-nuclear code quality review

Launch the `thermo-nuclear-code-quality-review-subagent` via the Task tool on the branch diff before completion.

Fix or explicitly defer every structural finding. Do not skip this step.
